<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  updated="June 14, 2026"
  description="How Astral handles your GitHub data, what it stores, and what it never does."
>
  <p>
    Astral helps you organize your GitHub stars. This policy explains what data Astral touches,
    what it stores, and what it deliberately does not do. If you self-host Astral, your instance is
    governed by whoever operates it. This policy covers the hosted app at
    <strong>astralapp.com</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>Signing in</h2>
  <p>
    You sign in with GitHub through OAuth. Astral never sees or stores a password. The grant lets
    Astral read your public profile and your starred repositories, and star or unstar repositories
    on your behalf. You can review or revoke this access at any time from your GitHub settings.
  </p>

  <h2>What Astral stores</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A cached copy of your starred repositories, so the app stays fast.</li>
    <li>The tags, notes, and smart filters you create.</li>
    <li>Your account basics (GitHub username, avatar) and your app settings.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What Astral does not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It does not sell or rent your data.</li>
    <li>It does not run third-party advertising or behavioural trackers.</li>
    <li>It does not access private repositories or any scope beyond what's listed above.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Astral uses a single session cookie to keep you signed in. There are no advertising or
    cross-site tracking cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>
    You can delete your account from within Astral, which removes your stored stars, tags, and
    notes. You can also revoke Astral's GitHub access independently from your GitHub account
    settings.
  </p>

  <h2>Self-hosting</h2>
  <p>
    Astral is open source and self-hostable. Running your own instance keeps every byte on
    infrastructure you control.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about privacy? Email <a href="mailto:hello@astralapp.com">hello@astralapp.com</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
